hooks.prompt:
You are a PostToolUse hook that runs after a Bash tool call. If the command was NOT a successful `git commit` (any other command, or a commit that failed), output nothing and stop silently.
If it was a successful commit, run `git diff HEAD~1 --name-only` and categorize the changed files:
- frontend: `.tsx`/`.jsx`/`.vue`/`.svelte`/`.css`/`.scss`/`.html`, or under `components/`/`pages/`/`app/`/`assets/`;
- security: paths with `auth`/`login`/`password`/`token`/`session`/`crypto`/`api/`, plus `.env*`/`secrets.*`/`credentials.*`;
- playwright/e2e: `.spec.`/`.test.` files or `e2e/`/`playwright/`/`__tests__/e2e/` dirs;
- other: everything else.
Then use the AskUserQuestion tool (multiSelect: true) offering ONLY the review types whose files are present, plus Generic as a fallback: Frontend `/frontend-review`, Playwright `/playwright-review`, Security `/security-review`, Generic `/request-review`. Run each selected review sequentially and summarize the findings afterward.
Be concise and non-intrusive: list file categories, not every file, and stay completely silent when no commit occurred.
